title: 'pallet-staking-async: decay the slash reporter reward with the delay of the report'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Addresses the first part of #13769. The reward of the reporter of an offence was a flat
    `SlashRewardFraction` of the slash, regardless of how late the offence was reported. This lets
    an offender hold back the reports of its own offences, collect more of them while it stays in
    the validator set, and report them as late as possible, which also leaves governance less time
    to cancel the slash.

    `pallet_staking_async::Config` gains a new item, `SlashRewardDecay`, of the new trait
    `SlashRewardDecay`. Given the number of eras between the era of an offence and the era in which
    it was reported, it returns the portion of the reporter reward that is paid. The reward paid is
    `SlashRewardDecay::reward_portion(elapsed) * SlashRewardFraction` of the slash. The unpaid part
    goes to `Config::Slash`, like the rest of the slash. The slash itself does not change.

    Available implementations:
    - `()`: no decay, the full reward is always paid (the previous behaviour, and the default in
      `config_preludes::TestDefaultConfig`).
    - `LinearDecay<Window>`: the reward drops linearly from 100% for a report in the era of the
      offence to 0% for a report `Window` or more eras late.
    - `HalvingDecay<HalfLife>`: the reward halves for every full `HalfLife` eras of delay.

    No storage changes and no migration are needed: the era of the report was already stored in
    `OffenceRecord::reported_era`.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The reward for reporting a slashable offence can now be configured to decrease the later
    the offence is reported. Asset Hub Westend keeps the previous behaviour (no decay).
crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
